"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Predicate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Input","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A predicate is a logical condition that evaluates to a Boolean value (true or false). You use predicates for operations like filtering a collection or searching for matching elements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To create a predicate, use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Predicate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro. For example:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let messagePredicate = #Predicate<Message> { message in","    message.length < 100 && message.sender == \"Jeremy\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the example above, the closure that contains the predicate’s conditions takes one argument — the value being tested. Even though you write the predicate using a closure, the macro transforms that closure into a predicate when you compile. The code in the closure isn’t run as part of your program."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the predicate’s definition, you can use the following operations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arithmetic ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"%","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unary minus ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Range ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"..."},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"..<"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Comparison ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<="},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":">"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":">=","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"!="},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ternary conditional ("},{"code":"?:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Conditional expressions","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Boolean logic (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"&&"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"||"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"!"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift optionals (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"?"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"??"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"!"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if"},{"text":"-","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let"},{"text":" expressions)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Types (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"as"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"as?"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"as!"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sequence operations ("